# Cloudflare Pages — redirects / clean-url fallback
# Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# Next.js static export produces flat *.html files. Cloudflare Pages clean-URL
# auto-resolves /foo → /foo.html by default. These explicit entries are an
# additional safety net for any edge case and guarantee correct 404 behavior.

# --- Permanent (301) slash normalization for static export ---
/:splat/  /:splat  301

# --- 404 fallback — Cloudflare Pages serves /404.html automatically on miss.
# This line acts as a no-op placeholder so Pages definitely treats 404's
# through this file instead of returning the Pages default 404 page.
/*  /404.html  404
